23:T735,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this the price my jeweller will charge?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. It is a spot-based India estimate. Jewellers add making charges, GST and their own margin, so the retail price is higher."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why does the silver rate change every day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It follows the global silver price and the USD/INR exchange rate, both of which move during the day."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between 999 and 925 silver?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"999 silver is 99.9% pure and common for coins and bars. 925 sterling silver has 92.5% silver mixed with other metals and is used for most jewellery because it is harder."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is silver a good investment?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Silver is volatile and can swing widely. It can diversify a portfolio, but it is not guaranteed to rise. This tool is for information, not investment advice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this the jeweller retail silver rate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We show a spot-based India estimate (international silver × USD/INR). Local jewellers add making charges and GST — confirm before buying."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the Silver Rate free on ContentVerse India?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. All India utility tools on ContentVerse India are free to use with no sign-up required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is this an official government website?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. ContentVerse India is an independent platform. We use public datasets and open APIs. For official records, use government portals like Parivahan, GST, FoSCoS, or ECI."}}]}24:T7bb,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to use Silver Rate","description":"Silver is bought as jewellery, coins, bars and as an industrial metal, and its price in India changes every day with global silver rates and the dollar–rupee exchange rate. This tool shows a spot-based estimate of the silver rate per gram, per 10 grams and per kilogram in India, and includes a weigh","url":"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/silver-rate","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"Silver Rate"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"How to use the silver rate tool","text":"Check the per-gram, 10-gram and per-kg figures at the top, then enter a weight in grams in the weight calculator. The tool multiplies the weight by the current estimated rate and shows the approximate value. For a kilogram, enter 1000 grams."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"What decides the silver price in India","text":"Three things drive the price: the international silver price quoted in US dollars per troy ounce, the USD/INR exchange rate, and Indian import duty and taxes. When the rupee weakens against the dollar, silver becomes more expensive in rupees even if the global price does not move."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Buying silver: purity, making charges and GST","text":"Pure silver is 99.9% (999 fine). Jewellery is usually 92.5% sterling silver (925). Ask for a hallmark or a purity certificate, and check the weight on a calibrated scale. Making charges for jewellery can range from a few percent to well over 15% of the metal value, and GST is charged on both the metal and the making charges."},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Estimate versus the rate at your jeweller","text":"Use this tool to know roughly what the metal is worth and to check whether a quoted price is in a sensible range. If a shop’s price is much higher than the estimate plus reasonable making charges and GST, ask for a breakup."}]}19:[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Silver Rate\",\"alternateName\":\"Silver Rate Today India — Price per Gram & Kg\",\"description\":\"Check today's silver rate in India per gram, 10g and kg. Spot-based estimate with weight calculator.\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/silver-rate\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"browserRequirements\":\"Requires JavaScript\",\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"INR\"},\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"ContentVerse India\",\"url\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-IN\",\"featureList\":\"How to use the silver rate tool, What decides the silver price in India, Buying silver: purity, making charges and GST, Estimate versus the rate at your jeweller\"}"}}],["$","script","1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$23"}}],["$","script","2",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"India Tools\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Silver Rate\",\"item\":\"https://contentverse.co.in/tools/silver-rate\"}]}"}}],["$","script","3",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$24"}}]],"$L25"]
